1] What are wrapper classes ?

Ans :- Wrapper class in java is object representation of primitive data types,
       They allowed primitive data types to be treated as objects,
       There are eight wrapper classes corresponding to Eight primitive data types
       they are present in java.lang package.

Sr   Wrapper-Class    Data-Type
1]   Integer          int
2]   Double           double
3]   Long             long
4]   Short            short
5]   Character        char
6]   Boolean          boolean
7]   Float            float
8]   Byte             byte


2] Why do we need Wrapper classes
Ans :- Collections like arrayList Only Stores Objects, Nullability,
       Primitive cannot store null values,
       Generics cannot deal with primitive data types.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

* Autoboxing :- Automatically converting primitive to its corresponding wrapper class
 Example :- int x= 101;
            Integer obj = x// Autoboxing Java Takes care in background

* Unboxing :- Unboxing automatic conversion of Wrapper class object to its primitive data type.

          Integer obj = Integer.valueOf(100); // Wrapper object
          int x = obj; // ✅ Unboxing: Integer → int
          System.out.println("Primitive int: " + x);

